      "card_ids": ["C61", "C62", "C63", "C64", "C65", "C66", "C67", "C68", "C69", "C70", "C71", "C72"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No matched oral versus IV AUC data for the query.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2, PAMPA, or human jejunal permeability data; L5 records are for reference molecules.",
    "No query-specific efflux transporter or intestinal metabolism experiment.",
    "C19 is a close but not identical analogue and its low-F outcome is qualitative.",
    "C70 shows lack of P-gp interaction for dabigatran, so efflux transfer to the query is uncertain."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low and strengthened: the query is a fully ionized zwitterionic benzamidine and carboxylate peptidomimetic with logD -7.48 and TPSA 148.6. The most transferable direct low-F context (C19) reports absolute oral bioavailability not high enough for oral use in humans for a similarly benzamidine and carboxylate rich molecule. L5 adds human jejunal P_eff values for related ionizable peptidomimetics (enalaprilat 0.013e-4 cm/s, inogatran 0.03e-4 cm/s) and a high efflux ratio of 46 for a related amidine and carboxylate compound, coherently supporting presystemic loss. Confidence stays moderate because all mechanistic records are for reference molecules, not the query."
}

